have to switch the bottles if you feel like your&nbsp;
column needs a deeper cleaning it would be best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:08.080
to do a reverse flush you start by disconnecting&nbsp;
the column at the low pressure end and then the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:14.080
high pressure end don't forget to remove the guard&nbsp;
lastly you flip the column around and you can flow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:19.840
into a container so you don't dirty your detector&nbsp;
the method for reverse flush would be to start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:28.720
with 95 percent water and 5 methanol for about 10&nbsp;column volumes. Then you do a gradient of 5% to 95%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:35.360
methanol for five column volumes and lastly&nbsp;
you hold five percent water and 95% methanol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.080
for 10 column volumes you want to run this at&nbsp;
half of your normal flow rates for your method&nbsp;&nbsp;

